# Source bytes must never depend on who checked out the repository.
# Migration SQL lives in C# raw string literals, so a CRLF checkout changes the
# migration checksums DnaX records in every database's ledger. That stranded the
# published 0.1.0 alphas; see docs/roadmap.md, "Migration ledger compatibility".
* text=auto eol=lf

# Redundant under the rule above, but kept explicit for the checksum-critical
# manifests so the intent survives any future change to that rule.
src/Monkeysphere.Data/Domains.cs text eol=lf
src/Monkeysphere.Data/MonkeysphereSchema.cs text eol=lf
src/Monkeysphere.Data/RemoteUploadSchema.cs text eol=lf
src/Monkeysphere.Data/*Migration.cs text eol=lf

# Byte-exact content that must never be normalized.
src/Monkeysphere.Web/wwwroot/vendor/** -text
tests/Monkeysphere.Web.Tests/Fixtures/*.monkeysphere-backup -text
